<title>USA: Maraven Cardon plant had small fire at unit.</title>
<headline>Maraven Cardon plant had small fire at unit.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuela's second largest refinery, the 286,000 barrels-per-day plant at Punta Cardon, had a small problem which didn't affect operations, sources said on Monday.</p>
<p>The Cardon plant, operated by the Maraven subsidary of state oil company Petroleos de Venezuela, had a brief fire at a hydro-desulphurisation unit, according to a market source.</p>
<p>The plant was operating normally on Monday, according to a source at Maraven.</p>
<p>--New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1620</p>
</text>
